<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 6 January, from 1066 to 1950.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/harold-godwinson" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harold-godwinson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1066">1066 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">960 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Harold Godwinson crowned King of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The day after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-confessor">Edward the Confessor</a>'s death, Harold was crowned, probably in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William of Normandy</a> disputed the succession and invaded that autumn, killing Harold at Hastings.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1205">1205 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">821 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Philip of Swabia is crowned a second time at Aachen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-of-swabia">Philip of Swabia</a>, elected King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in 1198, was crowned again at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a>, the traditional coronation site, by the Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a>, his former opponent. The repeated ceremony cleared the taint of his first coronation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-of-swabia">Philip of Swabia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1412">1412 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">614 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joan of Arc is born at Domrémy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By tradition <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a> was born on Epiphany in the village of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domremy-la-pucelle">Domrémy</a>, in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. She led French forces to relieve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a> in 1429, was burned in 1431 and canonised in 1920.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1838">1838 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">188 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alfred Vail and Samuel Morse demonstrate their telegraph</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Speedwell Ironworks in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a>, Vail and Morse sent messages over two miles of wire using an early form of their code. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">Telegraph</a> lines soon spread across America and the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">Telegraph</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1907">1907 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">119 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Maria Montessori opens her first Casa dei Bambini</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a tenement in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s San Lorenzo district, Montessori opened a 'children's house' for working families. The child-led methods she developed there spread to schools across the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1912">1912 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alfred Wegener presents his theory of continental drift</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At a geology meeting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a>, Wegener argued that the continents had once formed a single landmass and drifted apart. Long rejected, the idea was vindicated by plate tectonics in the 1960s.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1941">1941 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">85 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Roosevelt sets out the 'Four Freedoms'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In his State of the Union address, Franklin Roosevelt named freedom of speech, freedom of worship, freedom from want and freedom from fear as universal rights. The speech shaped Allied war aims and the UN.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1950">1950 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">76 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain recognises the People's Republic of China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The United Kingdom became the first major Western power to recognise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a>'s communist government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>. The decision, partly aimed at protecting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a>, split <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> from US policy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 6 January <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-ii-of-england"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Richard II of England</span><span class="tp">1367–1400</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gaspar-de-guzman-count-duke-of-olivares"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gaspar-de-guzman-count-duke-of-olivares.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gaspar de Guzmán, Count-Duke of Olivares</span><span class="tp">1587–1645</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-gaspar-rodriguez-de-francia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-gaspar-rodriguez-de-francia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Gaspar Rodríguez de Francia</span><span class="tp">1766–1840</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-schliemann"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/heinrich-schliemann.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Heinrich Schliemann</span><span class="tp">1822–1890</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/victor-horta"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/victor-horta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Victor Horta</span><span class="tp">1861–1947</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fan-noli"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fan-noli.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Fan Noli</span><span class="tp">1882–1965</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/norman-kirk"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/norman-kirk.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Norman Kirk</span><span class="tp">1923–1974</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 6 January <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gilbert-de-clare-1st-earl-of-pembroke"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gilbert-de-clare-1st-earl-of-pembroke.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gilbert de Clare, 1st Earl of Pembroke</span><span class="tp">c. 1100–1148</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/uzun-hasan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/uzun-hasan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Uzun Hasan</span><span class="tp">d. 1478</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alessandro-de-medici"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alessandro-de-medici.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alessandro de' Medici</span><span class="tp">1510–1537</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-iv"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mehmed-iv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mehmed IV</span><span class="tp">1642–1693</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gregor-mendel"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gregor-mendel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gregor Mendel</span><span class="tp">1822–1884</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/theodore-roosevelt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/theodore-roosevelt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Theodore Roosevelt</span><span class="tp">1858–1919</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/david-alfaro-siqueiros"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/david-alfaro-siqueiros.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">David Alfaro Siqueiros</span><span class="tp">1896–1974</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
